ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":136,"prev":29,"next":138,"titles":140,"firmware":23},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":6,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":17,"status":18,"firmware":19,"facts":24,"procedures":78,"parameters":92,"related":116,"body":119,"sources":120,"official_url":28,"controls":130},"tempo.tempo-screen","Tempo, tap tempo and metronome",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"bpm","tempo","tap tempo","metronome","click","speed","change tempo",0,"knowledge/manual/units/tempo/tempo-screen.md",{"modes":15,"screens":16},[],[6],"The tempo key opens the tempo screen from anywhere; tap it to set the tempo by ear. `E1` sets BPM, `E2` and `E3` the groove, `E4` the metronome level (click to switch the metronome on or off).","current",{"min":20,"changed_in":21,"guide_version":22,"verified_on":23},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15","1.1.33",[25,31,36,40,45,48,52,56,59,63,66,69,72,75],{"id":26,"text":27,"source":28,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":30},"open","`tempo` opens the tempo screen from any screen.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/tempo#project",null,"official",{"id":32,"text":33,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"range","The tempo runs from 40 to 220 BPM, the ends of the metronome weight's travel and of the range CC80 is held to.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#211-tempo","derived",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":23,"confidence":39},"tap","Tapping `tempo` repeatedly in time with the music sets the tempo.","verified",{"id":41,"text":42,"source":43,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":44},"tap-third","The tempo changes on the third tap, not the second; the unit takes the mean of the two gaps between three taps (one video, OS 1.1.x, taps about 0.58 s apart gave 104.5 BPM while the page kept showing 120 until after the third). The guide's picture shows four presses, which also works; a first and second tap alone do not change the tempo.","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":8,"text":46,"source":47,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":30},"`turn E4` sets the metronome volume and `click E4` switches the metronome on or off.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/tempo#edit-tempo",{"id":49,"text":50,"source":51,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":23,"confidence":39},"cc80","Over MIDI, CC80 on any channel sets the tempo; on OS 1.1.33 the result is twice the value in BPM, held within 40–220, so only even tempos can be sent.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-26--session-1-results-owner-present-scratch-project-os-1133",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":55,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"one-tempo","The tempo is one value for the whole project; it sits on no module page, so no parameter lock or LFO reaches it, and a tempo change over a song (a ramp) is made by hand on the tempo page, over MIDI (CC80), or by following an external MIDI clock.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sequencer#step-sequencing",{"id":57,"text":58,"source":51,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":23,"confidence":39},"new-project","A new empty project runs at 120 BPM (OS 1.1.33).",{"id":60,"text":61,"source":62,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"new-metronome","A new project starts with the metronome on, at about two thirds of its volume (the project file stores the click volume, with 0 for off).","docs/research/10-xy-format.md#32-projectsettings-0x00000x0094",{"id":64,"text":65,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":23,"confidence":39},"screen","The tempo page has a light background, the BPM as a large number on the left and a metronome in the middle carrying the groove type's two-letter abbreviation.",{"id":67,"text":68,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":23,"confidence":39},"weight","The metronome's weight slides down its arm as the tempo rises, from the top at 40 BPM to the bottom at 220.",{"id":70,"text":71,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":23,"confidence":39},"speaker","The speaker icon at the top right loses its sound waves as `E4` turns the metronome down.",{"id":73,"text":74,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":23,"confidence":39},"pendulum","While the sequencer plays, the pendulum swings from one end to the other on every beat, and the beat's dot below it lights; stopped, it rests at the left end with no dot lit.",{"id":76,"text":77,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"smear","The swinging pendulum looks smeared, as if it left trails; the copies come from the screen's slow response rather than being drawn.",[79,86],{"id":37,"goal":80,"preconditions":81,"steps":82,"result":29,"source":28,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":30},"Set the tempo by tapping",[],[83],{"keys":84,"note":85,"set":29},"tempo → tempo → tempo → tempo","tap in time with the beat",{"id":8,"goal":87,"preconditions":88,"steps":89,"result":29,"source":47,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":30},"Switch the metronome on or off",[],[90],{"keys":91,"note":29,"set":29},"tempo → click E4",[93,99,104,109,113],{"screen":6,"encoder":94,"layer":95,"keys":96,"name":6,"range":29,"default":29,"cc":97,"cc_confidence":30,"note":98,"source":47,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":30},"E1","base","turn E1",80,"song tempo in BPM",{"screen":6,"encoder":100,"layer":95,"keys":101,"name":102,"range":29,"default":29,"cc":29,"cc_confidence":29,"note":103,"source":47,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":30},"E2","turn E2","groove type","the style of swing (see grooves)",{"screen":6,"encoder":105,"layer":95,"keys":106,"name":107,"range":29,"default":29,"cc":29,"cc_confidence":29,"note":108,"source":47,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":30},"E3","turn E3","groove amount","right of centre adds swing, left of centre adds shuffle",{"screen":6,"encoder":110,"layer":95,"keys":111,"name":112,"range":29,"default":29,"cc":29,"cc_confidence":29,"note":29,"source":47,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on